 <datum name=title value="Bitwise Operations">
</metadata>
<manual>

<p>In the rare cases where you have to fiddle with the bits inside
integers, you can use the bitwise operations in Pike. They work just
like in C and C++, and if you need to use them, you probably already
know what they mean.</p>

<xtable>
<row><h>Operation</h>		<h>Syntax</h></row>
<row><c><p>Shift left</p></c>		<c><p>a &lt;&lt; b</p></c></row>
<row><c><p>Shift right</p></c>		<c><p>a &gt;&gt; b</p></c></row>
<row><c><p>Bitwise not</p></c>		<c><p>~ a</p></c></row>
<row><c><p>Bitwise and</p></c>		<c><p>a &amp; b</p></c></row>
<row><c><p>Bitwise or</p></c>		<c><p>a | b</p></c></row>
<row><c><p>Bitwise exclusive or</p></c><c><p>a ^ b</p></c></row>
</xtable>

</manual>
